# Upstream's own ignore conventions, kept as they are. Nothing below the first
# block is ours, and nothing in the second block removes an upstream entry to
# make room for a fork-owned one.
#
# zlib's release tarball ships no `.gitignore` at all, so the entries in the
# first block are upstream's *build system* outputs rather than upstream's
# ignore file, and they are listed here so a `make`-produced object or archive
# cannot be committed into a tree that is built with Zig instead. They are read
# out of `src/Makefile.in`: `OBJZ`/`OBJG` at `:59-60` name the `.o` files,
# `PIC_OBJZ`/`PIC_OBJG` at `:63-64` name the `.lo` files, and `:32-36` names
# `STATICLIB=libz.a`, `SHAREDLIB=libz.so`, `SHAREDLIBV=libz.so.1.3.2` and
# `SHAREDLIBM=libz.so.1`.
*.o
*.lo
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
*.la
*.dylib
*.dll
*.obj
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.def.bak
*.exe
*.map.bak

# Upstream's build-testing programs. `src/Makefile.in` links `minigzip` from
# `src/test/minigzip.c` and `example` from `src/test/example.c` for its `test`
# and `check` targets, and `infcover` from `src/test/infcover.c` for coverage.
# This package compiles none of them -- they stay in `src/` digested and
# unbuilt -- but a tree that ran upstream's `make test` must not commit them.
/minigzip
/minigzip.o
/example
/example.o
/infcover
/infcover.o
/zconf.h.in.bak
/zconf.h.bak
/zlib.pc.bak

# zig build artefacts (fork addition).
#
# These are directories rather than single files because a normal `zig build`
# creates them, and a normal `zig build` must not dirty the tree or leak into
# the package published from it. None of them is named in build.zig.zon
# `.paths`, so an ignored directory can never become part of the package.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/
# Zig 0.16 fetches dependencies into a project-local directory. This package
# declares no dependencies, so this exists only so that a future one cannot
# commit a fetched tree.
zig-pkg/

# The consumer package builds inside this repository and has its own cache and
# output tree. It is ignored here as well as in consumer/.gitignore so a build
# run from the repository root cannot commit it by accident.
consumer/.zig-cache/
consumer/zig-out/
consumer/zig-pkg/

# `smoke.zig` writes one gzip member into the working directory, reads it back
# and deletes it with a `defer`. The entry is here so that a run interrupted
# between the write and the delete -- a failed assertion, a Ctrl-C -- cannot
# leave a stray member behind for the next commit to pick up.
zlib-smoke-*.gz

# Nix and devenv working-tree artefacts (fork addition).
#
# `nix build` writes `result` (and `result-1`, `result-2`, ... on a rebuild)
# into the directory that asked for it, and `devenv` writes its resolved
# inputs and its state beside the project. None of them is named in
# build.zig.zon `.paths`, so an ignored path can never become part of the
# package either. `devenv.lock` and `flake.lock` are deliberately *not* here:
# they are real inputs, they belong to the driver, and ignoring them would be
# the wrong way to keep a build out of a commit.
result
result-*
.devenv/
.devenv.flake.nix
.devenv.flakes/
devenv.local.nix
.direnv/